  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTEGRATED ACTIONS FOR CLIMATE CHANGE ADAPTATION AND MITIGATION (IA-4-CCAM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at enhancing climate resilient smallholder agriculture through sustainable land management, advocacy and access to weather information, targeting 30 farmer-based organizations (comprising at least 50% female each).  Project activities include &#x2022; Evidence generation through action research and the intercropping of cassava and groundnut with minimum tillage as a novelty for climate change adaptation and mitigation in targeted communities.&#x2022; Capacity building of target farmers through enhanced knowledge and skills on intercropping as a means to achieving sustainable land management as well as improving productivity.&#x2022; Strengthening technical cooperation with SLMet and MAF in terms forecasting and analysis capacity</narrative>
  </description>
